From: System Electronics <info@systemelectronics.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wm8960: add opt-in automatic MCLK/PLL selection

Allow boards using simple-audio-card to request the WM8960 automatic
clock-selection mode through the wlf,sysclk-auto device-tree property.

This lets the codec first try the external MCLK directly and fall back
to its internal PLL when that clock cannot generate the requested audio
sample rate.

The behaviour is opt-in and therefore does not affect existing WM8960
users.

Signed-off-by: System Electronics <info@systemelectronics.com>
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wm8960.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wm8960.c
index 499604f..01a0694 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wm8960.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wm8960.c
@@ -128,0 +129 @@ struct wm8960_priv {
+	bool sysclk_auto;
@@ -1292,0 +1294,5 @@ static int wm8960_set_dai_sysclk(struct snd_soc_dai *dai, int clk_id,
+		if (wm8960->sysclk_auto) {
+			wm8960->freq_in = freq;
+			clk_id = WM8960_SYSCLK_AUTO;
+			break;
+		}
@@ -1415,0 +1422,5 @@ static int wm8960_i2c_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c,
+	if (i2c->dev.of_node)
+		wm8960->sysclk_auto =
+			of_property_read_bool(i2c->dev.of_node,
+					      "wlf,sysclk-auto");
+
